<kw name="Get Device Location" source="E:\Project\RobotFrameworkStandard\.venv\Lib\site-packages\AppiumLibrary\keywords\_applicationmanagement.py" lineno="434">
<arguments repr="">
</arguments>
<doc>&lt;p&gt;Gets the device's current GPS location with human-readable address information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Retrieves GPS coordinates from the connected device and performs reverse geocoding to convert coordinates into readable address components (country, state, city).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Returns: dict: Location data with the following structure:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;country&lt;/code&gt; (str): Country name or empty string if unavailable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;state&lt;/code&gt; (str): State/region name or empty string if unavailable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;city&lt;/code&gt; (str): City/town/village name or empty string if unavailable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;latitude&lt;/code&gt; (float): GPS latitude coordinate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;longitude&lt;/code&gt; (float): GPS longitude coordinate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Examples:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table border="1"&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;${location}=&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Get Device Location&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Log&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Current location: ${location['city']}, ${location['country']}&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Should Not Be Empty&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;${location['latitude']}&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Should Be True&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;${location['longitude']} != 0&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prerequisites:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Device location services must be enabled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;App must have location permissions granted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Internet connection required for address lookup&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uses OpenStreetMap's Nominatim geocoding service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</doc>
<shortdoc>Gets the device's current GPS location with human-readable address information.</shortdoc>
</kw>
<kw name="Get Device Time" source="E:\Project\RobotFrameworkStandard\.venv\Lib\site-packages\AppiumLibrary\keywords\_applicationmanagement.py" lineno="416">
<arguments repr="format: str | None = None">
<arg kind="POSITIONAL_OR_NAMED" required="false" repr="format: str | None = None">
<name>format</name>
<type name="Union" union="true">
<type name="str" typedoc="string"/>
<type name="None" typedoc="None"/>
</type>
<default>None</default>
</arg>
</arguments>
<doc>&lt;p&gt;Returns the date and time from the device.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Args:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;format&lt;/code&gt;: the set of format specifiers. Read &lt;a href="https://momentjs.com/docs/"&gt;https://momentjs.com/docs/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;to get the full list of supported datetime format specifiers. If unset, default return format is &lt;span class="name"&gt;YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ssZ&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Examples: ${device_time}    | Get Device Time | DD MM YYYY hh:mm:ss | ${device_time}    | Get Device Time | |&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Return: str: The date and time&lt;/p&gt;</doc>
<shortdoc>Returns the date and time from the device.</shortdoc>
</kw>
<kw name="Get Element Attribute" source="E:\Project\RobotFrameworkStandard\.venv\Lib\site-packages\AppiumLibrary\keywords\_element.py" lineno="407">
<arguments repr="locator, attribute">
<arg kind="POSITIONAL_OR_NAMED" required="true" repr="locator">
<name>locator</name>
</arg>
<arg kind="POSITIONAL_OR_NAMED" required="true" repr="attribute">
<name>attribute</name>
</arg>
</arguments>
<doc>&lt;p&gt;Returns the element attribute using the given &lt;code&gt;attribute&lt;/code&gt;, e.g. name, value, etc.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Examples:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table border="1"&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Get Element Attribute&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;locator&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;name&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Get Element Attribute&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;locator&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;value&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;</doc>
<shortdoc>Returns the element attribute using the given ``attribute``, e.g. name, value, etc.</shortdoc>
</kw>
<kw name="Get Element Location" source="E:\Project\RobotFrameworkStandard\.venv\Lib\site-packages\AppiumLibrary\keywords\_element.py" lineno="428">
<arguments repr="locator">
<arg kind="POSITIONAL_OR_NAMED" required="true" repr="locator">
<name>locator</name>
</arg>
</arguments>
<doc>&lt;p&gt;Returns the location of the element with the &lt;code&gt;locator&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key attributes for arbitrary elements are &lt;span class="name"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; and &lt;span class="name"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;. See &lt;a href="#Introduction" class="name"&gt;introduction&lt;/a&gt; for details about locating elements.&lt;/p&gt;</doc>
<shortdoc>Returns the location of the element with the ``locator``.</shortdoc>
</kw>
<kw name="Get Element Rect" source="E:\Project\RobotFrameworkStandard\.venv\Lib\site-packages\AppiumLibrary\keywords\_element.py" lineno="450">
<arguments repr="locator">
<arg kind="POSITIONAL_OR_NAMED" required="true" repr="locator">
<name>locator</name>
</arg>
</arguments>
<doc>&lt;p&gt;Returns the dimensions and coordinates of the element with the &lt;code&gt;locator&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key attributes for arbitrary elements are &lt;span class="name"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; and &lt;span class="name"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;. See &lt;a href="#Introduction" class="name"&gt;introduction&lt;/a&gt; for details about locating elements.&lt;/p&gt;</doc>
<shortdoc>Returns the dimensions and coordinates of the element with the ``locator``.</shortdoc>
</kw>
<kw name="Get Element Size" source="E:\Project\RobotFrameworkStandard\.venv\Lib\site-packages\AppiumLibrary\keywords\_element.py" lineno="439">
<arguments repr="locator">
<arg kind="POSITIONAL_OR_NAMED" required="true" repr="locator">
<name>locator</name>
</arg>
</arguments>
<doc>&lt;p&gt;Returns the size of the element with the &lt;code&gt;locator&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key attributes for arbitrary elements are &lt;span class="name"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; and &lt;span class="name"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;. See &lt;a href="#Introduction" class="name"&gt;introduction&lt;/a&gt; for details about locating elements.&lt;/p&gt;</doc>
<shortdoc>Returns the size of the element with the ``locator``.</shortdoc>
</kw>
<kw name="Get Matching Xpath Count" source="E:\Project\RobotFrameworkStandard\.venv\Lib\site-packages\AppiumLibrary\keywords\_element.py" lineno="477">
<arguments repr="xpath">
<arg kind="POSITIONAL_OR_NAMED" required="true" repr="xpath">
<name>xpath</name>
</arg>
</arguments>
<doc>&lt;p&gt;Returns the number of elements matching the &lt;code&gt;xpath&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;One should not use the &lt;span class="name"&gt;xpath=&lt;/span&gt; prefix for 'xpath'. XPath is assumed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table border="1"&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Correct:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;${count}&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Get Matching Xpath Count&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;//android.view.View[@text='Test']&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;Incorrect:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;${count}&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Get Matching Xpath Count&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;xpath=//android.view.View[@text='Test']&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you wish to assert the number of matching elements, use &lt;a href="#Xpath%20Should%20Match%20X%20Times" class="name"&gt;Xpath Should Match X Times&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</doc>
<shortdoc>Returns the number of elements matching the ``xpath``</shortdoc>
</kw>
<kw name="Get Network Connection Status" source="E:\Project\RobotFrameworkStandard\.venv\Lib\site-packages\AppiumLibrary\keywords\_android_utils.py" lineno="18">
